    description: "As the American Juicer: +2D4x10 to Spd."
  - name: "Super Reflexes and Reaction Time"
    description: "As the American Juicer: +2D4 to P.P. (minimum P.P. 20), +4 to initiative, +4 to roll with punch, fall or impact, two additional attacks per melee, and an automatic parry or dodge against all attacks, even from behind. Reduced penalties: meditation and breathing exercises let the ninja juicer hide the super-reflex jitters and appear a normal, relaxed person for 10 minutes per point of M.E. (M.E. 12 means two hours) before the pent-up tension gives him away."
  - name: "Enhanced Balance and Stealth"
    description: "A drug-enhanced sense of balance allows incredible acrobatic feats and near-silent movement. Can hold his breath for up to five minutes without penalty, even while running or fighting. Walks on rice paper without tearing it, crosses a narrow beam or tightrope as easily as solid ground, and is never made dizzy or afraid by heights or sudden movement. +15% to Climbing, Acrobatics and Prowl (not counting O.C.C. bonuses); if those skills are not taken, has them automatically at 45% +2% per level. Penalty: the grace and silence cannot be turned off - he sneaks up on most people automatically, which startles and frightens those around him and makes civilians suspicious."
  - name: "Saving Throw Bonuses"
    description: "Identical to the American Juicer: +4 vs psionics, +6 vs mind control, +8 vs toxins, poisons and drugs (in the bonuses above)."
  - name: "Enhanced Healing"
    description: "Same as the American Juicer: rapid healing, +20% to save vs coma and death, and virtual imperviousness to pain."
restrictions:
  - "Life span: the ninja juicer dies 6 years plus 2D6 months after the conversion. Only Juicer Detoxification (Rifts RPG p.69-70) can help, and a clan member may undergo it only with the clan''s consent; renegades who try are hunted down and killed."
  - "Cybernetics: starts with only the clan''s tracer chip. The clan may order one or two special implants (usually not before level 2 or 3); most ninja juicers take no others."
  - "Hand to Hand: Ninjitsu is not available."
  - "Cannot sustain a long-term infiltration: the drug harness, violent reactions to sudden movement and detectable implants give him away within hours."
side_effects: "Death 6 years plus 2D6 months after conversion. Years of meditation and breathing exercises spare the clan-trained ninja juicer the usual American Juicer penalties and manic stress, and let him mask his super-reflexes for 10 minutes per M.E. point; his constant, unshakeable silence and grace still unsettle ordinary people. A freelance assassin given the same conversion by H-Brand or Ichto without the ninja training suffers all the usual Juicer penalties."
extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 8: Japan printed 84-86 (cache p085-p087, text layer, page_offset +1). The Ninja Juicer description and Juicer Powers are on printed 84; the stat block is on 85, read off a render (the text layer drops Communications: Any (+5%)); equipment, money and cybernetics head printed 86. The chapter''s M.O.M./Crazies & Juicer Augmentation section (printed 74) is background and prices only and changes no number here. || GROUP: a Juicer conversion, stored as men-of-arms like every other Juicer; sdc_base is stated so no men_of_arms line is needed. || XP: the Ninja Borg, Ninja Crazy, Ninja Juicer column (printed Ninja Jucier) of the Experience Point Tables, printed 216 (cache p217), bottom of the third column, read off a render. It is identical to the standard Juicer''s stored ladder. || JUICER NUMBERS: the book says its powers are identical to the Rifts RPG p.69 Juicer unless noted. Stored as printed here: P.S. +2D4+2 with minimum 20, P.P. +2D4 with minimum 20, P.E. +2D6, Spd +2D4x10, S.D.C. 1D4x100, hit points +1D4x10, +4 initiative, +4 roll, +2 attacks. The saves are printed only as identical to the American Juicer and are copied from the catalog''s juicer row (RUE figures). The standard Juicer''s pull punch, perception and disarm bonuses are NOT stored: this class restates its reflex bonuses and does not print them. Automatic parry or dodge is prose. || SKILLS: Japanese stored as Language: Native Tongue at the catalog''s 98% (the book''s +15% cannot raise it further) and Literacy: Native Language at 40+10. Imitate Voice and Impersonation (+8%) is read as two skills, Imitate Voices & Sounds and Impersonation, each +8%. Climbing and Prowl carry both the +10% O.C.C. bonus and the +15% of Enhanced Balance and Stealth; Acrobatics is granted at the ability''s 45% +2% per level. The related-skills Rogue floor of two is stored as minimums. Secondary skills are limited as the related list, without its bonuses. || HAND TO HAND: Assassin, replaceable with Aikido, Jujitsu or Karate at no cost (costs 0); Ninjitsu is not available. || EQUIPMENT: the vibro-nail glove (3D4 M.D.) has no catalog row and is left in the note of the vibro-blade choice rather than stubbed. The micro-film camera is this book''s micro-film-camera row (printed 83); the class prints no crowbar. Not stored as gear rows: the bio-data implant and the unspecified choice of non-energy weapons. Money 1D6x1000 credits is stored; the 2D4x1000 credits'' worth of black market salable items is prose. || RACE: copied from the standard Juicer."
---

## Lore

H-Brand and a few other corporations use the outlawed Juicer conversion to build a shadow army of assassins. Unlike American Juicers, ninja juicers are neither desperate nor power-hungry: most are raised from childhood in the same hidden training camps as the tech-ninja, crazies and ''borgs, and are taught that their duty is to serve until their early death. Between the ages of 14 and 18, candidates with the right body and temperament - dedicated, usually not overly bright, and fanatically loyal - are chosen for conversion. They are taught that dying young is a glorious destiny; the brightest flame burns shortest.

Years of meditation and breathing exercises before the treatment lengthen the ninja juicer''s life to about six years plus 2D6 months and dampen the manic, stressed-out state of ordinary Juicers. Raising one costs well over three million credits, so a clan spends them carefully and never as cannon fodder, except in their last months. About one in ten who survive three years and prove their worth is rewarded with detoxification and conversion into a ninja ''borg.

Teams of 1D6 ninja juicers, or mixed teams with crazies and ''borgs, back regular tech-ninja on assassinations, raids and sabotage, always under a tech-ninja''s orders, as bodyguards, enforcers and strike teams. Their harnesses, their violent reactions to sudden movement and their detectable implants mean they can fool ordinary people for a few hours at most. Between missions they live in remote camps, training and playing as only Juicers can.

## GM Notes

A ninja juicer who rebels is marked for death by the clan, and the termination teams sent after him are often his fellow juicers. A player character''s escape can drag the whole group into conflict with the clan and carry a campaign.

H-Brand and Ichto also sell the basic ninja-juicer package, without the years of training, to mercenaries, criminals and anyone who can pay, sometimes for 2 or 3 years of service in the Otomo Army. These freelance assassins dress in black and call themselves ninja, but belong to no clan, are never offered detox or ''borg conversion, and suffer every usual Juicer penalty. They are best built as a standard Juicer.

## Equipment and Money

Besides the listed gear (which includes a micro-film camera that fits in the palm) the character gets bio-data implants, a choice of non-energy weapons, and a vibro-nail glove (3D4 M.D.) may be one of the two vibro-blades. Money: 1D6x1000 credits and 2D4x1000 credits'' worth of black market salable items. The clan may provide more for a mission and covers all living expenses; the ninja spends most of his life in hidden camps and headquarters.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ninja-juicer');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ninja-juicer';

